IdleXP End User License Agreement

Copyright (c) 2026 IdleXP. All rights reserved.

This is an agreement between you and IdleXP ("the holder"), regarding the
IdleXP software ("the software"). By installing or using the software, you accept these
terms. If you do not accept them, do not install and do not use it.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

The holder grants you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable
license to install and use the software on the computers you use, for your own
use. There is no time limit, no charge and no user account.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Without the prior written authorization of the holder, you may not:

  a) copy, publish, distribute or make available to third parties the
     installer, the executable or any part of the software;
  b) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the software;
  c) extract, decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the software, except
     as applicable law allows regardless of this agreement;
  d) sell, rent, lend, sublicense or charge in any way for the software or for
     access to it;
  e) remove or alter authorship notices, trademarks or this license notice.

3. OWNERSHIP

The software is licensed, not sold. The holder retains all rights to it,
including to the source code, which is not published. Possessing a copy of the
software, or having access to the repository in which it is developed, grants
no license to the source code.

4. RELATIONSHIP WITH HUNTERA

IdleXP is not produced, endorsed, sponsored by or affiliated with Huntera
(https://huntera.com.br/) or whoever operates it. "Huntera" and the game's
trademarks belong to their respective owners.

The software only reads the game: it does not automate gameplay actions.
Complying with Huntera's terms of use and rules is the responsibility of the
player, and using the software does not change that responsibility.

5. PRIVACY

The software has no server and no account, and sends none of your data to the
holder. There is no sign-up, telemetry, analytics, advertising or tracker.

Everything it keeps stays on your computer, in the %APPDATA%\idlexp folder:
the game logins, your preferences and a technical log (diagnostico.log), which
is never sent anywhere. Uninstalling the software does not delete that folder.

The software talks only to Huntera itself, to the login service Huntera uses
and, each time it opens, to GitHub, to check whether a new version exists.
The request to GitHub carries only what any download carries, the IP address
of your connection, and the versions involved: nothing about you, your
computer or your accounts. The privacy notice published with each version
describes each item in detail.

6. WARRANTY AND LIABILITY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN
ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION
WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

7. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The software embeds third-party components, each under its own license, which
prevails over this one as to that component:

  Electron          — MIT license
  ws                — MIT license
  electron-updater  — MIT license, with the libraries it uses, under the
                      MIT, ISC, Blue Oak 1.0.0 and Python 2.0 licenses
  Barlow            — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (text in
                      src/renderer/assets/fonts/OFL.txt)

8. TERMINATION

This license terminates automatically if you fail to comply with any condition
above. Once terminated, you must stop using the software and uninstall it. You
may terminate it at any time by uninstalling the software.

9. GOVERNING LAW

This license is governed by the laws of Brazil.

10. FUTURE VERSIONS

A future version of the software may come with a different license. That
license applies to the version it accompanies; this one continues to apply to
